POLICIES

OCRA Policies

The Obstacle Course Racing Association of Ireland (OCRA ÉIREANN) maintains policies and procedures designed to support the safe, fair and responsible development of obstacle sport.

These policies apply alongside the OCRA Constitution, Bylaws and applicable competition rules.

Why Policies Matter

Obstacle sport involves athletes, children and young people, coaches, Technical Officials, clubs, race organisers, volunteers and many other participants.

Clear policies help everyone understand the standards expected within OCRA activities and what processes apply when an issue arises.

Our Policy Areas

OCRA's governance and integrity framework includes areas such as:

- Safeguarding
- Anti-Doping
- Codes of Conduct
- Complaints and Disciplinary Procedures
- Equality and Inclusion
- Data Protection
- Athlete welfare
- Conflicts of interest
- Competition integrity
- Safety
- Other organisational policies as required

